    <!--
      The set-type CHIP marks: the work set is the drawn dot, the other three take the first
      letter of their own name in the current language (§26, "Set types take their first letter").
      New — no mockup draws a mark for the three non-work types, so this is a decision and not a
      transcription; the chip keeps its 34x32 and takes no other treatment, the letter occupying
      exactly the dot's place. They shipped as HARDCODED ENGLISH LITERALS inside AppSetTypeChip
      until the editors stage, which is why a Russian build drew W for разминка.
      `..._mark_work` is the same glyph in every language and is a resource anyway, so the four
      marks live in one table rather than three plus a literal.
    -->
    <string name="core_ui_kit_set_type_mark_warmup">W</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_set_type_mark_work" translatable="false">·</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_set_type_mark_failure">F</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_set_type_mark_drop">D</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_setbar_add">+ set</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_setbar_remove">− set</string>
    <!--
      The discard SHEET's four strings (§26, "Every modal on the three editors is a SHEET").
      They live in the kit because one component now serves all three editors and each of them
      used to carry its own copy — three tables saying the same thing is how «Отмена» survived on
      one screen after being renamed on another. The Russian is the drawing verbatim
      (`pass2d.html` `#s-editor` form 3); the English follows it rather than the old wording.

      «Продолжить правку», not «Отмена»: the old label read as CLOSING THE WINDOW rather than as
      declining to discard, which is the wrong thing to promise on the gentle branch.
    -->
    <string name="core_ui_kit_discard_sheet_title">Leave without saving?</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_discard_sheet_body">Unsaved edits will be lost.</string>
    <string name="core_ui_kit_discard_sheet_confirm">Leave without saving</string>
